    "message": "Check arrivals and departures on the shared generated Scenario\n\nThese tests took the small replay fixture and, for some, hand-added a\nfloor plan without facility awareness. The ones that only need people\narriving, leaving or stepping out now use the shared generated Scenario\n(#88), so arrivals and departures also go through the awareness\nupdates a UI Scenario has:\n\n- a departure or a temporary exit/transfer interrupts the open action;\n- an arriving household's context reaches behaviour, frames and\n  checkpoints;\n- a departure admits the next waiting household member (the sleeping\n  area holds 21 with 20 residents, so one of two arrivals waits);\n- arrivals fill a surveyed overflow room when their areas are full.\n\nTwo tests stay on hand-built worlds and say why: the demand coupling\nneeds cleaning staff the generator never creates (#75), and arrival\napproach routes are an operator input it never makes.\n\nThe tests move next to the modules they check: population.py,\npopulation_lifecycle.py and common_operations.py.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
