    "message": "Check runtime floor-plan changes on the shared generated Scenario\n\nEleven tests took the small replay fixture and hand-added a toy floor\nplan (every zone the same square, every facility at one point) without\nfacility awareness. They now use the shared generated Scenario (#88):\nequipment transfers, route closures, temporary rooms and beds, and the\ntrips they replan. Coordinates come from the generated geometry, and\nwhere a test pinned a toy-plan value it now checks the relationship\n(a service point moves by the facility's offset).\n\n- Generated plans have one route per area, so the reroute test adds a\n  slower route through the same doors and registers it on them.\n- Generated people carry minute-by-minute psychological state, so the\n  hand-driven tests advance one minute at a time.\n- The partition test queues on a split-queue toilet so the partition\n  clears the declared passage; it ends with a TickEngine run and moves\n  to tests/integration/test_effect_program_geometry.py, now checking\n  that its queue empties.\n\nThe nine tests without a floor plan (preflight, facility modifiers,\nguards, structural additions, operational handlers) keep the small\nfixture as component tests and join tests/unit/events/test_effects.py.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
